276    /** FUNCTION otap_string.is_sys_object
277    * Analyze names for typical system objects. Identifier is beginning SYS_ for system generated object and $ or #,
278    * which may occur anywhere in the name of system objects. Oracle strongly discourages the use of the symbols $ and # in object names.
279    *
280    * Usually used in NOT constructs like WHERE NOT otap_string.is_sys_object(object_name, 1).
281    *
282    * @param p_string The string to analyze if it is a system object starting with SYS_ or containing a $ sign.
283    * @param p_exclude Switch to turn the check off when set to 0. Default is 1. Other values interpreted as 1. If set to 0 will always return FALSE.
284    *
285    * @return TRUE if string is a system object, otherwise FALSE (also on errors).
286    */
287    FUNCTION is_sys_object( p_string  IN VARCHAR2
288  			     , p_exclude IN NUMBER   DEFAULT 1
