456    /** FUNCTION otap_test.has_constraint
457    * Checks if a given table has a constraint of the given type. Optional you can specify column and constraint name.
458    *
459    * Supported constraint types:
460    * C - Check constraint on a table
461    * P - Primary key
462    * U - Unique key
463    * R - Referential integrity - use has_ref_constraint for more options
464    * V - With check option, on a view
465    * O - With read only, on a view
466    * H - Hash expression
467    * F - Constraint that involves a REF column - use has_ref_constraint for more options
468    * S is not supported, could not find or create an example to examine. SUPPLEMENTAL LOG clause only reflects in CDEF$ and CCOL$.
469    *
470    * @param p_table_name Mandatory. The table to be checked for constraint, take as is. Case sensitive. Missing value will cause test to fail.
471    * @param p_constraint_type Mandatory. A valid constraint type. Not case sensitive. Wrong values will cause the test to fail.
472    * @param p_column_name Optional. The column that is part of the constraint. Case sensitive.
473    * @param p_constraint Optional. The name of the constraint. Case sensitive.
474    * @param p_schema A schema override of the current test session if needed, taken as is. If given the table and constraint must exist in this schema. Case sensitive.
