524    /** FUNCTION otap_test.has_not_null_constraint
525    * Checks if a given table column has a not null check constraint. Optional you can specify the constraint name. NOT NULL constraint is
526    * somewhat special as it is recommended for inline creation, which generates system constraint names. You are also free to create it
527    * outbound. Therefore in most cases the constraint name is not defined or may change on recreation. Also NULLABLE may not reflect an
528    * existing outbound NOT NULL constraint. This function checks also the definition, which has the generated format: "COLUMN_NAME" IS NOT NULL.
529    * Any outbund declaration will probably look different. Therefore the term "IS NOT NULL" and the column name is searched after UPPER conversion
530    * of SEARCH_CONDITION_VC. Will not work for search conditions > 4000 char.
