825    /** FUNCTION otap_test.alike
826    * Checks given data of type VARCHAR2 against an Oracle LIKE expression. LIKE is currently more reliable and easier
827    * to use than Oracle REGEX implementation. But also much more limited.
828    *
829    * @param p_have The data to check.
830    * @param p_like A valid Oracle like expression that p_have must match.
831    * @param p_case_sensitive Optional defines that the compared result is handled as case sensitive, if set to otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE.
832    * @param p_description The test description if any. If not given, a description is generated, see template.
833    * @param p_expected_result The expected test result as number. Default is test passed. See otap_constants.
