848    /** FUNCTION otap_test.throws_ok
849    * Checks if a given statement or code block throws the expected error message. The expected error message must match
850    * the SQLERRM returned from exception thrown. Use throws_match or throws_like if only parts of the error message must
851    * match. If the statement starts with SELECT it is executed as is, without caring for returned columns or rows and ignoring
852    * any given header definition. The header definition is a code block for the declare section defining variables that may be
853    * needed by called functions or procedures. It is only used if the statement does not start with SELECT and if the declaration
854    * block can be executed with a NULL procedure without throwing exceptions.
855    *
856    * Function comes in two flavors, comparing SQLERRM as VARCHAR2 or the error code SQLCODE as number. It can also be used to check
857    * if a statement does not cause any exception by switching the expected result to otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_FAILED.
858    *
859    * SQL statements (SELECT, UPDATE, DELETE) MUST NOT have a trailing semicolon. otap will try to detect and remove it, but may fail.
860    * Semicolon in dynamically executed SQL statements will cause an unexpected exception.
861    *
862    * Functions and procedures MUST have a trailing semicolon, especially if more than one command is executed in the block.
863    *
864    * Syntax errors will most likely cause a different exception as the expected one and fail the test. This is especially important if
865    * you switch the expected test result. otap expects in this case, that the statement could be executed without any exception.
866    *
867    * @param p_statement Mandatory. The statement as string to execute. Can be a select statement or function/procedure call. No need to proovide a begin end block. Syntax should be checked or will cause unexpected exceptions.
868    * @param p_sqlerrm Mandatory. The exact case sensitive expected error message as returned by SQLERRM after a provoked exception.
869    * @param p_header_def Optional valid header definition (test result is undefined if header is not valid) for function or procedure tests to support OUT and return variables.
870    * @param p_description The test description if any. If not given, a description is generated, see template.
871    * @param p_expected_result The expected test result as number. Default is test passed. See otap_constants.
872    * @param p_schema A schema override of the current test session if needed, taken as is. Compares are not clearly associated to a schema. Case sensitive.
873    *
874    * @return The test result as text.
875    *
876    * Examples (english messages)
877    * SELECT otap_test.throws_ok('SELECT 1/0 FROM dual', 'ORA-01476: divisor is equal to zero') AS test_result FROM dual;
878    * SELECT otap_test.throws_ok('l_return := 1/0;', 'ORA-01476: divisor is equal to zero', 'l_return NUMBER;') AS test_result FROM dual;
879    */
880    FUNCTION throws_ok( p_statement	     IN VARCHAR2
881  			 , p_sqlerrm	     IN VARCHAR2
882  			 , p_header_def      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
883  			 , p_description     IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
884  			 , p_expected_result IN NUMBER	 DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_PASSED
885  			 , p_schema	     IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA')
886  			 )
887  	 RETURN VARCHAR2
888    ;
