1025  	/** FUNCTION otap_test.generate_schema_tests
1026  	* Generates the test scripts for the current available otap schema functions using by default the current
1027  	* schema. Test set gets defined as schema, group represents the object types, like tables, triggers and so on.
1028  	* No translation provided. Limited to line size 4000 but not to rows, like DBMS_OUTPUT. It is up to you how you
1029  	* spool the content to files.
1030  	*
1031  	* Including system generated objects is a good idea if your system is stable and you want to ensure that no one
1032  	* changed the current state. With CI/CD or during development, when objects get recreated, it is a really bad idea.
1033  	* Excluded by default are objects beginning with SYS_ for system generated object or containing $ or # chars, which
1034  	* may occur anywhere in the name of system objects.
1035  	*
1036  	* There is no best option, some constraints like NOT NULL must be defined inline to count a column as NOT NULL.
1037  	* With an additional added constraint, the column will be still marked as NULLABLE. Identity columns are another
1038  	* issue, as you cannot define a name for the generated sequence. Make extra tests limited on the system generated
1039  	* objects you rely on (like NOT NULL and identity).
1040  	*
1041  	* @param p_like_schema The LIKE expression for schema names. Default is current schema. % will generate for all schemas in the database, be careful. Underlying objects are not limited. Case sensitive.
1042  	* @param p_required_user An optional comma separated list of users required to be checked by the schema test. Will not include the selected schemas. Useful for specific schemas and integration tests.
1043  	* @param p_title_prefix An optional title prefix for set, group and test names. Limited to 10 chars. Will be added without delimiter to the processed schema.
1044  	* @param p_show_header Used to surpress header comments, init, count and finish section. Default 1 will contain all sections, otherwise skipped.
1045  	* @param p_excl_sysgen Used to ignore system generated objects identified by SYS_, # or $. Default 1 will ignore system generated objects, otherwise included.
1046  	*
1047  	* @return An OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_REC object as table type OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_TBL.
1048  	*/
1049  	FUNCTION generate_schema_tests( p_like_schema	IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA')
1050  				      , p_required_user IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
1051  				      , p_title_prefix	IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
1052  				      , p_show_header	IN INTEGER  DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE
1053  				      , p_excl_sysgen	IN INTEGER  DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE
1054  				      )
1055  	  RETURN otap_view_result_tbl PIPELINED
1056  	;
1057  
